    {"file":"packages/foundation/modeling/yaml/src/YamlNode.ts","symbol":"QuoteCompat","kind":"literal-kit","owner":"@beep/yaml","identity":"QuoteCompat","description":"Foreign resolution dialects the stringifier's plain-scalar fallback can defend against: setting the `quoteCompat` field of `YamlStringifyOptions` to `\"yaml-1.1\"` additionally quotes every plain scalar a YAML 1.1 parser (js-yaml, PyYAML, libyaml, and the `yaml` npm package's YAML 1.1 schema, whose lenient resolvers set the outer bound) would implicitly resolve to a non-string — `yes`/`no`/`on`/`off` booleans, ISO 8601 and space-separated timestamps, sexagesimal `1:30`, underscored `1_000` and base-2/8/16 numbers. Like `QuoteStyle` it is a stringify-option vocabulary, never a property of a composed node."},
    {"file":"packages/foundation/modeling/yaml/src/YamlNode.ts","symbol":"QuoteStyle","kind":"literal-kit","owner":"@beep/yaml","identity":"QuoteStyle","description":"Quote characters available to the stringifier's plain-scalar fallback: the style a `plain`-styled scalar is rendered in when it turns out to require quoting. `auto` picks per value like the `yaml` npm package's default (single quotes for a value holding a double quote and no single quote, double quotes otherwise) and leaves an interior tab plain. Referenced by the `quoteStyle` field of `YamlStringifyOptions`; unlike `ScalarStyle` it is a stringify-option vocabulary, never a property of a composed node."},
